107.5,100) lies on the horizontal /OUT segment at identical y with full width overlap. Flagged informationally because the connectivity is positional rather than topological, which is a known maintenance hazard."},{"id":"PHY-03","title":"Geometry probe emitted repeated pcbnew assertion failures","location":"work/geometry/console.log","condition":"The geometry probe console contains three 'assert \"m_choices.GetCount() > 0\" failed in PROPERTY_ENUM()' messages from kicad/include/properties/property.h(607), and execution.json records a non-empty stderr hash, yet the check exited 0 and was recorded as pass.","mechanism":"Debug assertions firing inside the pcbnew Python bindings indicate the tool ran in a partially inconsistent state; a successful exit is not proof the extraction was complete, so the pass verdict rests on tool output that showed internal errors.","severity":"info","assessment":"concern","evidence":[{"path":"work/geometry/console.log","locator":"lines 2-4 (PROPERTY_ENUM assertion failures)"},{"path":"work/geometry/execution.json","locator":"stderr_sha256 ecfdabc9... (non-empty stderr), exit_code 0"}],"reasoning":"I independently re-derived the geometry result from the native board file: exactly five segments, all width 0.25 mm, matching geometry.json's counts, widths, pad list, and via. The assertions therefore did not corrupt this run's data, but the tool-health signal should be known to the operator since future runs on larger boards might not be so easily hand-verified."},{"id":"PHY-04","title":"vout_5ms measurement carries no acceptance limits","location":"packet criteria rc-step / work/rc-step/ngspice.log","condition":"The rc-step criterion declares two measurements but only vout_1ms has min/max bounds; vout_5ms (measured 0.9932621 V) has min and max of null, so it cannot fail.","mechanism":"An unbounded measurement adds no verification power: a gross error visible only in the settled value (for example a leakage path or wrong divider that still happens to pass the 1 ms window) would be recorded but never flagged. The 1 ms window alone does constrain R*C tightly (0.62-0.65 V maps to roughly tau = 0.93-1.05 ms), so coverage of the declared requirement 1 is real, but the settled-value check is decorative.","severity":"info","assessment":"concern","evidence":[{"path":"work/rc-step/ngspice.log","locator":"vout_5ms = 9.932621e-01 with no limit comparison"},{"path":"inputs/requirements/fixture-requirements.md","locator":"requirement 1 (only the 1 ms window is specified)"}],"reasoning":"This matches the declared requirement, which only bounds the 1 ms point, so it is not a defect; I recorded it because the review brief asks for independent challenge of verification coverage and stimuli. I confirmed the measured 5 ms value equals the analytic 1-e^-5 for the intended RC, so the unloaded response is in fact correct."}]},"ttft_ms":119606,"type":"result","duration_ms":178085,"uuid":"01ebb9f7-f391-4038-9c32-f9483ad9a472","ttft_stream_ms":2834,"time_to_request_ms":281,"first_content_frame_ms":2834,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
